== The new test (v2 -> v3) ==
EnclosureTests.test_tail_upper_endpoint_dominates_a_finer_midpoint_lower_bound   kills M06_CEILING_ONLY (C270-A4). Oracle: convexity of the tail integrand on [1,1/rhi] (CONTROLLED_FALSIFICATION.md 'Direct tail' paragraph: midpoint lower / trapezoid upper sums, 'It is convex; f''<=99/32*t^(-19/4)'; gates tail_convexity, tail_second_derivative) => trapezoid sums are upper bounds, midpoint sums lower bounds increasing under dyadic refinement. Asserts, at j=1 with CORE_PANELS patched to 64 (tail sums never read the core; tail_interval identical at 64 and 2^16 core panels, see proto3.log) and TAIL_PANELS at the declared 512 vs 2*512: (a) coarse tail upper endpoint >= finer tail lower endpoint [the kill]; (b) finer lower <= finer upper; (c) coarse lower <= finer lower + finer arithmetic tail_lower width (rigorous form of 'midpoint sums increase under refinement'); plus status INCONCLUSIVE_PRECISION (normalized_width gate fails with 64 core panels), tail gates true, evaluation counts 2114 / 4162, pc.TAIL_PANELS == 512.
Observed margins (proto3.log): pristine coarse upper - finer(1024) lower = +2.2415e-7; damaged (M06_CEILING_ONLY) coarse upper - finer(1024) lower = -7.4717e-8, exactly finer - damaged = 110770127964024035006453969387323164636630381124117933425519677/1482521263040042663009052462615821307352825354839967634589869622165504 == C270's rational. At 2048 panels the margins would be +2.0547e-7 / -9.3397e-8 (not used; 1024 reproduces C270's acceptance evidence at half the cost).
Runtime of the new test alone (python3.12, from the package dir): normal Ran 1 test in 0.623s ; -O Ran 1 test in 0.701s

